+# Invite and pre-C1 claim age exclusion — 2026-11-22
+
+- Invitation/activation eligibility uses the unchanged #615 `evaluateDiscoveryAge` calendar policy through inviteAge: patient-ID roster DOB only, America/New_York, adult on the 18th birthday, existing leap-day/date/year semantics. Valid under-18 or retained explicit dependent-minor marker yields MINOR; missing/unusable/impossible/future DOB yields DOB_UNKNOWN. No caller age/email identity fallback or force/config bypass.
+- `issueClaimToken(patientId,cohort)` retains its signature, response/TTL/schema/live-token contract; its mint transaction now reads the patient and checks age with fresh server time on each retry before token creation. All mint callers are covered: inviteOne, direct adminIssueInvite, birthday sweep and CLI. Shared sendInviteEmail resolves patient ID from the server token row and repeats the same age check immediately before transport; CLI direct transport uses that same preflight.
+- Manual and batch invite eligibility runs before reset-and-invite preparation/revocation; pure resumeReset and reset implementation remain untouched. #601/#602 suppression-before-cooldown order, force restrictions, new_invite routing, caps and wave gates stay unchanged. Initial minor/unknown refusal does not revoke existing invitations. DOB correction between an adult mint and send can block delivery; no promise of atomic mail recall or retrospective prevention of an already-authorized adult mint.
+- Manual age refusal: existing error envelope, HTTP409 FAILED_PRECONDITION with details.reason MINOR/DOB_UNKNOWN. Batch/auto canonical skip counters exclude age refusals from sends/reissues/failures/cap; late auto skips settle the current sending marker without incrementing consecutive failures or auto-stop. Birthday conversion/guardian consent code is unchanged; inviteSkipped records refusal. CLI dry/live/sandbox exclude/count holds, with existing confirmation, transport and override semantics.
+- `onboardingClassifier` removes its weaker UTC/impossible-date arithmetic and uses #615. Existing buckets, terminal/claim/shared-email ordering, dependent-minor exclusion and lowercase classifier report reasons remain compatible; invite adapters expose canonical uppercase reasons. Separate social age policy is unchanged.
+- **Claim addition approved with this same release:** after existing DOB match/audit and BEFORE any acquireWork/C1 reservation, claimAccount applies the same age precondition to roster DOB. Correct-DOB minors and valid-shaped unknown calendar DOB return HTTP403 PERMISSION_DENIED with MINOR/DOB_UNKNOWN. Missing/malformed roster DOB fails closed as DOB_UNKNOWN because identity verification cannot proceed. Incorrect submitted DOB keeps existing mismatch/throttle behavior. No account creation/credential update/enable/bind/token consume/session/hydration on age refusal, including pre-existing live-token claims. #619 C1/C2/receipt/lease/mint ownership logic, #617/#618 reset/provenance/holds and all claim-security helpers remain unchanged.
